        <div class="do-box"><b>The system design practice method:</b> (1) Set a 45-minute timer. (2) Pick a system from the list. (3) Spend 5 min on requirements and estimation. (4) Spend 10 min on high-level architecture diagram. (5) Spend 20 min on deep dive into 2-3 critical components. (6) Spend 10 min on scaling, failure modes, and monitoring. Do this 2-3 times per week. Record yourself explaining your design -- watch the recording and note where you hesitate. That hesitation is your study target.</div>
