      <div class="track-title">Low-Level Programming -- C, Assembly, Memory, Kernels, Drivers, Compilers</div>
      <div class="track-sub">Low-level programming is where you learn what the machine actually does. No garbage collector. No runtime. No abstractions hiding the truth. When you allocate memory, you free it. When you access an array, you calculate the address. When you write a driver, you talk to hardware registers. This knowledge makes you dangerous in any language because you understand what every abstraction is hiding.</div>
