              <div class="res-desc">The DDIA of machine learning. Covers the entire ML lifecycle in production: data engineering (data collection, labeling, feature engineering), model development (model selection, training, evaluation), model deployment (online prediction, batch prediction, edge deployment), monitoring and maintenance (data distribution shifts, model degradation, retraining triggers), and infrastructure (feature stores, model stores, ML platforms). Every ML engineer should read this cover to cover.</div>
