        <div class="insight"><b>The distributed training landscape:</b> Data parallelism (each GPU gets a copy of the model, different data batches -- PyTorch DDP). Model parallelism (model is split across GPUs -- Megatron-LM, DeepSpeed). Pipeline parallelism (model stages on different GPUs, micro-batches pipelined -- GPipe). For LLMs, all three are combined: FSDP (Fully Sharded Data Parallelism) + tensor parallelism + pipeline parallelism. Understanding these patterns is what separates ML scientists from ML engineers who train at scale.</div>
