              <div class="res-desc">A concise book (180 pages) on managing software complexity. Core ideas: deep modules (simple interface, complex implementation), information hiding, define errors out of existence, design it twice, comments should describe things that are not obvious from the code. Ousterhout's CS190 course at Stanford is built around this book. Read this alongside Clean Code -- they complement each other. Where Clean Code focuses on code-level practices, Ousterhout focuses on design-level thinking.</div>
